# Shopify Accessibility Implementation Guide

Apply these accessibility standards when developing or auditing Shopify stores to ensure WCAG 2.1 AA compliance and ADA adherence.

## Core Accessibility Requirements

### Image Accessibility
Always provide meaningful alt text for images that convey information, empty alt text for decorative images.

**Demo Pattern:**
```
Line 12: <img src="..." alt="{{ product.featured_image.alt | default: product.title }}">
Line 15: <img src="..." alt="" role="presentation"> <!-- decorative -->
Line 18: <img src="..." alt="{{ shop.name }} logo">
```

**Check in:** `sections/product-*.liquid`, `snippets/product-card.liquid`, `sections/hero-banner.liquid`

### Keyboard Navigation
Ensure all interactive elements are keyboard accessible with visible focus indicators.

**Demo Pattern:**
```
Line 34: *:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #0066cc; outline-offset: 2px; }
Line 41: button:focus-visible { box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(0, 102, 204, 0.3); }
```

**Requirements:** Tab order follows logical flow, all interactive elements focusable, visible focus indicators

### Color Contrast Standards
Maintain WCAG 2.1 AA contrast ratios: Normal text (4.5:1), Large text (3:1), UI components (3:1)

**Demo Pattern:**
```
Line 61: .text-primary { color: #0066cc; } /* 7.05:1 ratio */
Line 62: .text-muted { color: #6c757d; }   /* 4.54:1 ratio */
```

**Test with:** WebAIM Contrast Checker

### Semantic HTML Structure
Use appropriate HTML elements for their intended purpose.

**Demo Pattern:**
```
Line 73: <button type="submit">Add to Cart</button> <!-- not <div> -->
Line 77: <h1>{{ product.title }}</h1> <!-- proper hierarchy -->
Line 82: <header role="banner">
Line 84: <main id="main-content">
```

### Form Accessibility
All form inputs must have associated labels and proper error handling.

**Demo Pattern:**
```
Line 95: <label for="ContactFormName">Name *</label>
Line 96: <input id="ContactFormName" aria-describedby="name-error">
Line 103: <div id="name-error" role="alert">Error message</div>
```

### ARIA Implementation
Use ARIA attributes to enhance semantic meaning for screen readers.

**Demo Pattern:**
```
Line 118: <div role="dialog" aria-labelledby="cart-title" aria-modal="true">
Line 125: <button aria-label="Close cart drawer">
Line 132: <div aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" class="sr-only">
Line 139: <fieldset><legend>{{ option.name }}</legend>
Line 145: <input aria-describedby="variant-price">
```

**Check in:** `snippets/cart-drawer.liquid`, `sections/product.liquid`, `snippets/product-form.liquid`

