Line 245: alt="{{ product.title }}" aria-describedby="loading-status">
Line 246: <div id="loading-status" class="sr-only" aria-live="polite">Image loading...</div>
```

### Progress Indicators
Show progress for long operations to keep users informed and reduce abandonment during extended processes.

**Accessibility Impact:** Progress indicators are crucial for users with disabilities who may need more time to complete tasks. Screen reader users need progress announcements. Visual progress indicators must have programmatic equivalents.

**Key Requirements:**
- Progress bars must use `role="progressbar"` with proper value attributes
- Progress updates should be announced to screen readers
- Provide both percentage and descriptive progress information
- Allow cancellation of long-running operations
- Include estimated completion times when possible
- Progress indicators should be keyboard focusable for status checking

**Common Issues Solved:**
- Users abandoning long operations without progress feedback
- Progress information only available visually
- Unclear progress status for screen reader users
- No way to cancel or pause long operations
- Progress indicators without meaningful completion estimates

**Implementation Considerations:**
- Use `aria-valuenow`, `aria-valuemin`, and `aria-valuemax` for progress bars
- Implement live region updates for progress announcements
- Provide both determinate and indeterminate progress indicators
- Consider progress persistence across page refreshes
- Include contextual information about what's being processed
- Test progress indicators with various assistive technologies

**Demo Pattern:**
```
